 "result_text": "`Chain.from_json(chain.to_json())` now works for chains that contain predicates. I checked it with a smaller version of your example (node `name='a'`, `e_forward` with an `is_in` match on column `x`). The round trip returned the same JSON, and the `IsIn` predicate came back as `{'type': 'IsIn', 'options': ['a', 'b']}`. I did not run your exact Cayman Islands example or the test suite.\n\nThe cause was in `maybe_filter_dict_from_json` in `graphistry/compute/ast.py`. It called `ASTPredicate.from_json` on the base class, which tried to build the abstract base instead of the right subclass like `IsIn`. It now calls the existing type-dispatching `from_json` in `graphistry/compute/predicates/from_json.py`.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
